// scrml.dev /reference/errors/E-CHANNEL-INSIDE-PAGE
//
// Reference page for E-CHANNEL-INSIDE-PAGE. `<channel>` is not permitted inside `<page>`.
//
// SPEC anchors: §38.1, §38.4.1, §38.9, §40.8, §34.
//
// Written 2026-07-26. Prose derived from the compiler's own emission message in
// compiler/src; the reproducer below is the exact source compiled against the
// linked compiler to verify what this code does.

<page>

    // REFERENCE SIDEBAR opt-in — static, page-scoped, zero JS. The nav is
    // authored once in app.scrml and hidden by default; this shows it and
    // marks THIS page's link active. See scripts/gen-reference-nav.mjs.
    #{
        /* !important is load-order, not laziness: the shell's app.css is linked
           AFTER this page's stylesheet, so its `.refnav{display:none}` default
           wins at equal specificity. */
        .ref-shell { display: grid !important; }
        .refnav { display: block !important; }
        .refnav-link[data-ref="errors/E-CHANNEL-INSIDE-PAGE"] {
            color: rgb(125 211 252);
            background-color: rgb(14 165 233 / 0.10);
            border-left-color: rgb(56 189 248);
            font-weight: 600;
        }
    }

    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-3xl">

        <header class="not-prose mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200">
            <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mb-2">
                Reference &rsaquo; Errors
            </div>
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-rose-700 font-mono">
                E-CHANNEL-INSIDE-PAGE
            </h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 mt-2">
                <code>&lt;channel&gt;</code> is not permitted inside <code>&lt;page&gt;</code>.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4 text-xs">
                <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-rose-50 text-rose-700 rounded font-semibold">
                    Error
                </span>
                <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 rounded">
                    Compile-time
                </span>
                <a href="https://github.com/bryanmaclee/scrml/blob/main/compiler/SPEC.md#38"
                   class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                    SPEC §38.1 (normative)
                </a>
            </div>
        </header>

        <div class="rounded-lg border border-rose-300 bg-rose-50 px-5 py-4 text-slate-800 mt-8">
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
                <strong>NOT CURRENTLY EMITTED — verified 2026-07-26 against v0.7.1.</strong> This code is registered in the §34 catalogue but <strong>no walker fires it</strong>. The compiler source says so directly (<code>symbol-table.ts</code>: <em>"the error code is registered in §34 now but no walker fires it yet"</em>) and the probe below confirms it: a <code>&lt;channel&gt;</code> inside a <code>&lt;page&gt;</code> compiles clean and the build reports <em>"WebSocket channels: 1 channel(s) wired"</em>. The rule above is the specified behaviour and the shape you should write; it is simply not enforced today, so nothing will stop you getting it wrong. Reported upstream.
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            What it means
        </h2>

        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Channels are program-scoped: they own a WebSocket route for the whole application, not for one route within it. Declaring one inside a <code>&lt;page&gt;</code> implies a per-page channel lifetime the runtime does not provide. The canonical placements are inside <code>&lt;program&gt;</code>, or at file top in a pure-channel module file.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            Minimal reproducer
        </h2>

        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            This is the exact source compiled against the linked compiler to establish the behaviour described above. Read the callout at the top of this page before using it &mdash; it does <strong>not</strong> produce <code>E-CHANNEL-INSIDE-PAGE</code>.
        </p>

        <p class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mt-4 mb-1">app.scrml</p>
        <pre class="bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-md text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>&lt;program title="p"&gt;
    &lt;outlet/&gt;
&lt;/&gt;</code></pre>
        <p class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 mt-4 mb-1">pages/index.scrml</p>
        <pre class="bg-slate-900 text-slate-100 p-4 rounded-md text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>&lt;page&gt;
    &lt;channel name="chat"&gt;
        &lt;messages&gt; = []
    &lt;/&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;$&#123;@messages.length&#125;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/&gt;</code></pre>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            How to fix
        </h2>

        <ol class="space-y-3 text-slate-700 list-decimal list-outside ml-6">
            <li>
                <strong>Move the channel into <code>&lt;program&gt;</code>.</strong>
                Declare it once at program scope and read its cells from any page.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Use a pure-channel module file.</strong>
                A file with no <code>&lt;program&gt;</code> element may declare a <code>&lt;channel&gt;</code> at file top and export it.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            Related
        </h2>

        <ul class="space-y-1 text-slate-700">
            <li>
                <a href="/reference/elements/channel" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">&lt;channel&gt;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="/reference/elements/page" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">&lt;page&gt;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="/reference/errors/E-CHANNEL-OUTSIDE-PROGRAM" class="text-rose-700 hover:text-rose-900 underline">E-CHANNEL-OUTSIDE-PROGRAM</a>
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-4">
            Specification
        </h2>

        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Normative text: <strong>§38.1, §38.4.1, §38.9, §40.8, §34</strong>. Spec lives at
            <a href="https://github.com/bryanmaclee/scrml/blob/main/compiler/SPEC.md"
               class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                compiler/SPEC.md
            </a>.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-10 text-sm">
            <a href="/reference" class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 underline">
                &larr; Reference
            </a>
        </p>

    </article>

</>
